  "projects": [
    {
      "summary": "Five layers: a Rust CLI that does all the I/O, a link-grammar syntactic parser, an SWI-Prolog symbolic engine with no I/O, domain vocabulary packs kept as data, and some fifty Rust action binaries — a new verb is one pack fact and one binary. Mutation-tested, with a corpus of regression sentences and a cold start around 120 ms."
    },
    {
      "summary": "Nine pipeline stages (download → ocrize → parse → normalize → chunk → embed → retrieve → rerank → generate), each a port whose algorithm is chosen by label (BM25F, RM3, MMR, LambdaMART, TextRank…); hexagonal + DDD + TDD, standard library only in the core, no LLM. Metrics match pytrec_eval exactly. On six BEIR datasets no retriever wins everywhere (ndcg@10 0.668 on SciFact with BM25F); a LambdaMART reranker lifts ArguAna from 0.301 to 0.527 in 5-fold cross-validation."
    },
    {
      "summary": "A Rust workspace whose pure domain core (hexagonal, DDD, test-first) drives a terminal UI (ratatui) and Dioxus desktop and iOS apps: Leitner boxes with SM-2 scheduling over SQLite, content from checksummed data packs. Its data lab builds the six-language lexical database in Python — about 8,900 word senses (October 2026) aligned on WordNet, illustrated with Tatoeba sentences, analysed with spaCy, every word-in-sentence link checked."
    },
    {
      "summary": "A Python engine (DDD, hexagonal) weighs fifteen match-outcome strategies — Elo, Poisson attack/defence, form, head-to-head, squad value, rest days, bookmaker odds — adjusted for venue, and is ported to Rust/Dioxus apps for web (WebAssembly), desktop, mobile and terminal, kept at parity with it. A research lab backtests the strategies walk-forward, one tournament held out at a time, on 635 matches from ten tournaments (World Cups 2002–2022 and four continental cups of 2023–2024), and tunes the ensemble weights; out of sample, Elo alone scores best (55.6% accuracy)."
    },
    {
      "summary": "Internal platform that lets parliamentary staff search, explore and converse with the archives of the Belgian Federal Parliament, powered by a retrieval-augmented pipeline with bilingual FR/NL support."
    },
    {
      "summary": "Open, reproducible protocol that benchmarks retrieval strategies on the bilingual Senate corpus, measuring FR/NL robustness across the retrieval pipeline."
    },
    {
      "summary": "Backend: a modular monolith in Rust, split into bounded contexts with a hexagonal architecture, CQRS and an event-driven core (event store, outbox/inbox), served over REST/JSON and gRPC streaming; a PostGIS pipeline turns OpenStreetMap data into routing graphs published to a CDN, and custom Dylint lints enforce the architecture in CI. App: an offline-first Flutter client for iOS, Android, web and desktop — a Melos monorepo with Riverpod over an encrypted local store (Drift, SQLCipher), end-to-end encryption through a Rust core (vodozemac via flutter_rust_bridge), Bluetooth peer-to-peer sync, MapLibre maps and LiveKit real-time media. Website: a React single-page application built with Vite and internationalised with i18next."
    },
    {
      "summary": "MSc dissertation « Un cadre computationnel multicritère pour l'exploration de projections spatio-temporelles dans des systèmes sociaux complexes », UMONS Service d'Algorithmique — the R&D of Acteble's planning engine. Multi-objective group formation under spatio-temporal constraints: NP-hard by reduction from k-CLIQUE; admissible groups enumerated as bicliques (Close-by-One); an iterative Pareto solver with termination and local-convergence guarantees; one DSL compiled to Python, MiniZinc and Rust that yield bit-identical fronts, the Rust output running in the Acteble API. Benchmarked against CP-SAT, NSGA-II, MOEA/D and SPEA2 (hypervolume, IGD, 30 seeds, Wilcoxon–Holm): significantly ahead of MOEA/D at every size, of NSGA-II and SPEA2 from 500 users."
    },
    {
      "summary": "AI powered visual assistant for visually impaired people providing them with a description of their environment, OCR, code scans (QR codes & barcodes), and an adapted Valhalla routing system for the visually impaired."
    },
    {
      "summary": "Reminiscence application allowing people with cognitive issues to recover their memories through descriptions of their photos powered by facial recognition and LLMs. DeepFace by Serengil was used for the facial recognition pipeline."
    },
